<example>
# Good: Centralized Constants and Configuration
```java
// Single source of truth for validation constants
public final class ValidationConstants {
    public static final boolean DEFAULT_FROM_CACHE = false;
    public static final boolean DEFAULT_VALIDATE_FLAG = true;
    public static final String DEFAULT_SOCIAL_SEC_NR = null;
    
    public static final String VALIDATION_SUCCESS_MESSAGE = "Container validated successfully";
    public static final String VALIDATION_FAILED_MESSAGE = "Container validation failed";
    public static final String VALIDATION_ERROR_PREFIX = "Validation service error: ";
    
    private ValidationConstants() {} // Prevent instantiation
}

// Centralized file extension utilities
public final class FileExtensionUtils {
    public static final String ASICE_EXTENSION = ".asice";
    public static final String PDF_EXTENSION = ".pdf";
    
    public static String ensureAsiceExtension(String filename) {
        return filename.toLowerCase().endsWith(ASICE_EXTENSION) ? filename : filename + ASICE_EXTENSION;
    }
    
    public static String generateContainerFilename(String uid, Container.DocumentType type) {
        return uid + "." + type.name().toLowerCase();
    }
}
```
*Explanation: Centralized constants and utility methods prevent magic strings and duplicate logic.*
</example>

